```
ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: yellow
REAL_USE_CASE: Agent serving system designers (Parrot 2405.19888, Autellix 2502.13965) and KV cache researchers characterizing workload pressure; not production cost optimizers. Useful when debugging why prefix caches fill (tool-result text is 65.7% CC / 77.0% Codex of D1 token mass) and identifying heavy-tailed whale results for potential caching.
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: Microbenchmark-only for cost and latency wins. Token-mass majority (CC 0.657 LB95 0.569, Codex 0.770 LB95 0.748) collapses under cost-weighting to CC 0.198/0.025 and Codex 0.273/0.040 at 10x/100x decode $/tok (SplitWise/DistServe), so prefill caching saves <20% of dollars at best and <3% at 100x. DistServe 2401.09670 and SplitWise 2311.18677 already assume prefill-heavy; this measurement confirms direction but does not change the dollar optimization target (decode). Paged kernels (vLLM-APC 2309.06180, RadixAttention 2312.07104) already handle prefix caching; tool-result-specific routing adds complexity without demonstrated cost advantage in production.
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [Tool results are dynamic and context-specific, limiting cross-request reuse; heavy-tail (Gini CC 0.863, Codex 0.749) and HHI-by-session (CC 0.166, Codex 0.016 <0.20) prove within-trace concentration but not cross-user hot spots. CC static prompt is documented lower bound (4.5%, system prompt absent from logs) so measurement incomplete. Missing on-node chat baseline (flagged in packet) prevents validating divergence from chat regime where prefill may also dominate. Operational definitions rely on char/4 proxy, not tokenizer-exact counts.]
RATIONALE: Majority is real on conservative D1 (CC 0.657 LB95 0.569, Codex 0.770 LB95 0.748) with session-median corroboration (CC 0.573, Codex 0.757) and cross-instrument replication (|d|=0.113 <0.40). Heavy-tail is robust (top-decile CC 0.788 LB95 0.618, Codex 0.579 LB95 0.545; Gini CIs exclude 0.5). However, FIX-1 explicitly reports token-mass-not-dollar: cost-share collapses to 2.5-27.3%, making the operational win microbenchmark-only. The negative result is actionable guidance (do not over-invest in prefill caching for cost), but the granular decomposition does not by itself unlock a production deployment win beyond what RadixAttention/vLLM-APC already provide for prefix caching. Adoption requires evidence of cross-user reuse and a complete static/dynamic split (CC system prompt missing).
```
